# T91 — npm pack/publish walks .gitignore files it finds in the tree even when a package.json's
# `files` field explicitly lists a directory, so orchestrator/.gitignore's `dist/` rule (correct
# for git — dist/ is a build artifact, never committed) would otherwise silently strip the
# compiled CLI out of the tarball too. A directory's own .npmignore replaces its .gitignore for
# packing purposes, so this file exists purely to *not* say "dist/" — everything else that
# shouldn't ship (node_modules, test output, source maps for a dev-only build) still shouldn't.
node_modules/
coverage/
*.test.js
*.test.d.ts
*.test.d.ts.map
*.tsbuildinfo
